---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base title="About AI Eval Work Guide and how we source facts" description="How AI Eval Work Guide checks AI training platforms: official sources only, dated checks, no invented pay figures, no testimonials and no earnings promises." path="about/">
  <PageHead title="About AI Eval Work Guide" eyebrow="About" />
  <div class="wrap read"><div class="prose">
    <p>AI Eval Work Guide helps beginners understand paid AI training and evaluation work: what it is, which platforms offer it, what they ask for, and what they publish about pay.</p>
    <h2>How we source</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every requirement and pay figure comes from the platform's own official pages or a reputable source such as a government consumer agency. Each page links its sources and shows the date we last checked.</li>
      <li>We show pay only when the platform publishes it. If a platform does not publish a figure, we say so and show none.</li>
      <li>When official pages disagree (for example two help articles with different country lists), we say so and link both.</li>
      <li>We only list a platform once we can verify it from official pages.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What we don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We don't promise work or earnings, and we don't publish testimonials or income claims.</li>
      <li>We aren't affiliated with any platform listed, and we don't sell courses, accounts or "placement".</li>
      <li>We never ask you for money or personal documents.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Spotted something out of date? The official platform page always wins, and we update pages as terms change.</p>
  </div></div>
</Base>
